{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "ZEC.6.NIV"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/ZEC/6-fa3310a224463c6d2d07de7e698fced3.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/ZEC/6-fa3310a224463c6d2d07de7e698fced3.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bkZEC\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch6\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6\">\n            <div class=\"label\">6</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">A Vision of Four Chariots</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">Again I lifted my eyes and saw, and behold, four chariots came out from between two mountains. And the mountains were mountains of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Dan. 2:39</span></span><span class=\"content\">bronze. </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"content\">The first chariot had </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 1:8; Rev. 6:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">red horses, the second </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rev. 6:5</span></span><span class=\"content\">black horses, </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">the third </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 1:8; Rev. 6:2</span></span><span class=\"content\">white horses, and the fourth chariot dappled horses&#8212;all of them strong.</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">6:3 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">and the fourth chariot strong dappled horses</span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">Then I answered and said to </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 1:9</span></span><span class=\"content\">the angel who talked with me, &#8220;What are these, my lord?&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">And the angel answered and said to me, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 104:4; Heb. 1:7 </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;These are going out to the four winds of heaven, after </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 3:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">presenting themselves before </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 4:14</span></span><span class=\"content\">the Lord of all the earth. </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"content\">The chariot with the black horses goes toward </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 8; ch. 2:6; Jer. 1:13 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the north country, the white ones go after them, and the dappled ones go toward </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 9:14]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the south country.&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">When the strong horses came out, they were impatient to go and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 1:10]</span></span><span class=\"content\">patrol the earth. And he said, &#8220;Go, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 1:10]</span></span><span class=\"content\">patrol the earth.&#8221; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 1:10]</span></span><span class=\"content\">So they patrolled the earth. </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">Then he cried to me, &#8220;Behold, those who go toward </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 6 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the north country have set my Spirit at rest in </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 6 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the north country.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Crown and the Temple</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">And the word of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> came to me: </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Take from the exiles </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ver. 14] </span></span><span class=\"content\">Heldai, Tobijah, and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Neh. 7:39 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Jedaiah, who have arrived from Babylon, and go the same day to the house of Josiah, the son of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Kgs. 25:18</span></span><span class=\"content\">Zephaniah. </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"content\">Take from them silver and gold, and make a crown, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 3:5] </span></span><span class=\"content\">and set it on the head of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 3:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">Joshua, the son of Jehozadak, the high priest. </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"content\">And say to him, &#8216;Thus says the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> of hosts, &#8220;Behold, the man whose name is </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 3:8 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the Branch: for he shall branch out from his place, and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Matt. 16:18; Heb. 3:3]; See Eph. 2:20-22</span></span><span class=\"content\">he shall build the temple of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">. </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 12 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">It is he who shall build the temple of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 21:5; Ezek. 21:27 </span></span><span class=\"content\">and shall bear royal honor, and shall sit and rule on his throne. And there</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">6:13 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">he</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> shall be a </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 110:4; Heb. 3:1 </span></span><span class=\"content\">priest on his throne, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Hag. 2:9]</span></span><span class=\"content\">and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.&#8221;&#8217; </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"content\">And the crown shall be in the temple of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> as </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ex. 12:14; [Matt. 26:13; Mark 14:9] </span></span><span class=\"content\">a reminder to </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ver. 10] </span></span><span class=\"content\">Helem,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">6:14 </span><span class=\"ft\">An alternate spelling of </span><span class=\"fq\">Heldai </span><span class=\"ft\">(verse 10)</span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 10</span></span><span class=\"content\">Tobijah, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 10</span></span><span class=\"content\">Jedaiah, and Hen </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 10</span></span><span class=\"content\">the son of Zephaniah.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.14\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"ZEC.6.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Isa. 57:19; [Eph. 2:13, 19]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;And those who are far off shall come and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Isa. 60:10 </span></span><span class=\"content\">help to build the temple of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">. </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 2:9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">And you shall know that the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> of hosts has sent me to you. </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Deut. 30:1-3</span></span><span class=\"content\">And this shall come to pass, if you will diligently obey the voice of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> your God.&#8221;</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["ZEC.7"], "human": 